# Vendor-agnostic open GPU stack — Mesa with Vulkan/VA-API.
# GPU-ONLY: the builder copies this file for GPU roles (be+gpu / omnibus / edge_ai
# and every client desktop); headless pki/be/fe roles skip it (the role-independent
# container/iptables flags now live in package.use/containers, which is always copied).
#
# NO video_cards_* TOKENS HERE. The card set is a per-build decision made exactly
# once, by --gpu-driver, and rendered into make.conf's VIDEO_CARDS; mesa (and
# libdrm, and every other package with a video_cards_* IUSE) inherits THAT list.
# Forcing cards here instead pulled in each forced card's dependency chain while
# its deps kept inheriting the narrower make.conf list — unsatisfiable, and it
# aborts the whole 'image' emerge GROUP. This file used to force the all-free set
# (amdgpu radeonsi intel iris nouveau), which is why it went unnoticed: be+gpu and
# omnibus default to --gpu-driver all-free and agreed by accident, while edge_ai
# (default --gpu-driver nvidia ⇒ VIDEO_CARDS="nouveau nvidia") walled on
#   ">=x11-libs/libdrm-2.4.121[video_cards_amdgpu]" ... required by media-libs/mesa
# ~40min into the 2026-08-22 fleet run, reported as a missing grub/dracut/kubelet
# payload. build-x86-host-stage4.sh's assert_spec_video_cards() now refuses such a
# spec at argv time, and tests/scripts/test-spec-use-parity.sh pins it.
media-libs/mesa vulkan vaapi vdpau gles2 gbm egl llvm
media-libs/libva vaapi
